**Code Explanation:**

The code performs a joint analysis to investigate the relationship between the global Void Probability Function (VPF) 'leakage' and the local Gibbs (Strauss) repulsion parameter gamma across the 10 realizations. First, it loads the Strauss parameters computed in Step 3. Since the parameters were saved as a flat array across all qualifying halos, the script reconstructs the per-realization grouping by counting the number of qualifying halos (host mass > 10^13 M_sun/h, exactly 1 central, >= 3 satellites) in each realization. If the total count matches the length of the saved array, it partitions the array directly to compute the mean gamma per realization. If there is a mismatch, it falls back to re-running the exact parameter estimation logic with the same random seed to ensure consistency. Next, it loads the VPF results from Step 2. The VPF deviation metric for each realization is defined as the mean normalized residual across all radial bins: <(P0_empirical(r) - P0_Poisson(r)) / P0_Poisson(r)>_r. This metric captures the degree to which the empirical void hierarchy deviates from the Poisson expectation. Finally, the script performs a linear regression between the VPF deviation metric and the mean Strauss gamma parameter. It computes and prints the Pearson and Spearman correlation coefficients along with their p-values, and generates a scatter plot with the linear regression fit to visualize the correlation between global hierarchy leakage and local dynamical exclusion.

